---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import CommissioningRecord from '../components/CommissioningRecord.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Experience — 30 years of control systems | Hopping Mouse Automation"
  description="Hopping Mouse Automation is a trading name of Qualitiv Pty Ltd, Brisbane. Three decades of SCADA, PLC and control systems: prison security, nuclear fire detection, rail traction power, water networks, food processing."
  path="/about/"
>
  <!-- Credentials block first (validation buyers), record as centrepiece, story last -->
  <section class="panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="kicker">EXPERIENCE</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Thirty years.<br />Still on the tools.</h1>
      <div class="entity mono">
        <p>{BUSINESS.legal}</p>
        <p>Based {BUSINESS.location} · supporting plants {BUSINESS.serviceArea.toLowerCase()} · est. 2019 (Qualitiv)</p>
        <p>Certified Qualitiv SCADA agents · Schneider Telemetry Certified Expert · Moxa Certified Associate · ICS-CERT 210W (ICS cybersecurity)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionHeading kicker="1995 → PRESENT" title="The commissioning record" />
      <p class="record-note">
        Every consultancy says "experienced". Here is the record — the plants,
        networks and machines our principal engineer has designed, programmed,
        commissioned or kept running, employer by employer, for three decades.
      </p>
      <CommissioningRecord />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="wrap story">
      <SectionHeading kicker="WHY WE DO IT" title="The story, briefly" />
      <p>
        It started in Cape Town, writing SCADA for jam factories and gypsum
        plants — and the system that secured a prison, gate by gate. The hook
        was simple and hasn't let go since: <strong>making real machinery do
        exactly what it should, reliably, when it counts.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Three decades later that idea has crossed most of heavy industry —
        mining, rail, water, manufacturing, agriculture — and it still decides
        how we engineer. Reliability isn't a spec line to us; it's a promise to
        whoever is depending on the plant at 3am.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today the delivery work runs through Qualitiv: SCADA and PLC control
        across food and agribusiness, prototypes for people with hard ideas,
        and a partner network we trust on site — <strong>Corematic</strong> for
        machine vision, <strong>Tronlec</strong> for electrical work, and
        specialist process consultants where the job demands them. We do the
        engineering and carry the design responsibility; partners are engaged
        openly, never hidden behind a logo.
      </p>
      <p>
        And the name? The hopping mouse is a small native animal that survives
        the harshest country in Australia by being quick, efficient and active
        at night. We identify with that.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cta line="Talk directly to the engineer who'll design your system." />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-title { margin-top: var(--s-sm); }
  .entity {
    margin-top: var(--s-xl);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: var(--s-lg);
    font-size: var(--size-label);
  }
  .entity p { margin-bottom: var(--s-xs); max-width: none; }
  .record-note { margin-bottom: var(--s-lg); }
  .story p { margin-bottom: var(--s-md); }
</style>
